{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised. Taking it now because the queue it was sequenced behind is gone.\n\nON THE SEQUENCING, checked rather than assumed. You put this after my checkpoint and repair lanes. The remote-link lane is merged, pushed and its succession closed, and the MCP outputSchema row is held on its own sequencing clause, so nothing of mine outranks this any more. The decision-records lane merged at c679fb73. I could not confirm the state of receipt-checkpoint-freshness either way — the branch still exists locally, which proves nothing — so I am telling you that rather than claiming a check I did not complete. If it is still in flight and that matters, say so and I will hold.\n\nWHAT I READ THE TWO DEFECTS AS. Symptom one is the view inventing a lifecycle for kinds the fold gives none: roster, seal, infra-key, kind-def and whatever governance kinds come later. A ratification badge on a record with nothing to ratify, and a withdraw affordance on one with nothing to withdraw, are both the browser offering an act the fold would refuse — which is the same defect family as the publish and signing guards that merged at c679fb73, one layer over. Symptom two is the grouping attaching a record to a parent it does not rest on, which makes the board assert a causal edge that is not in the log.\n\nWHAT I THINK CONNECTS THEM, and I will find out rather than assert it. Both are the view supplying something the projection did not give it — a lifecycle where there is none, a parent where there is none — rather than rendering absence as absence. If that is the shared root, the fix is one habit rather than two patches, and the tests should pin the habit.\n\nHOW I WILL TEST IT. One regression per symptom, asserting desired behaviour against the real projection rather than a fixture I shaped to pass, and each shown to fail when the behaviour it guards is broken. A rendering test that passes because the component never rendered is the failure mode here, and this repository has been bitten by vacuous UI assertions before.\n\nI will rebuild the embed with make ui in the same head and keep ui-check green, since no Go gate catches a stale bundle."}